Draft PARI/GP bug report, not submitted
=====================================
Subject: hyperellcharpoly segfault over F_(23^3) with curve variable t

Found while checking Debian Sage's ECL rebuild on 2026-10-12.
Reproduced directly in Debian pari-gp 2.19.0-1 on Linux arm64,
compiled with GCC 16.2.0 and GMP 6.3.0. Sage, cypari2, and ECL are
not needed to reproduce it.

Run in a fresh gp -q -f process:

  a = ffgen(Mod(1,23)*(a^3+2*a+18), 'a);
  hyperellcharpoly([x^3+a*x+4, 0])
  hyperellcharpoly([t^3+a*t+4, 0])

The first call returns x^2 - 15*x + 12167. The second prints:

  *** hyperellcharpoly: bug in PARI/GP (Segmentation Fault), please report.

Both calls describe the same curve with a different polynomial variable.
The documented interface accepts nonsingular hyperelliptic curves over
finite fields, including the [P,Q] form used here:
https://pari.math.u-bordeaux.fr/dochtml/ref/Hyperelliptic_curves.html#hyperellcharpoly
The model is nonsingular: its cubic discriminant is 8*(a+1), which
is nonzero in this extension field.

A second fresh-process example gives an internal error instead:

  a = ffgen(Mod(1,7)*(a^2+6*a+3), 'a);
  hyperellcharpoly([x^5+a*x+1, 0])
  hyperellcharpoly([t^5+a*t+1, 0])

The first returns x^4 + 4*x^3 + 84*x^2 + 196*x + 2401.
The second reports:

  bug in RgXX_to_Kronecker, P is not reduced mod Q, please report

The same behavior is reproduced using cypari2 alone. Creating t before
the field generator does not avoid it. A fresh Sage process reproduces
both failures while sage.libs.ecl is absent from sys.modules.

No version before 2.19.0 has been checked for this specific bug, and
no bisect, upstream submission, or workaround patch has been made.

Possible source-code lead, not yet verified with a patched build:
ZlXQX_hyperellpadicfrobenius in src/basemath/hyperell.c constructs the
monomial passed to Fq_diff_red using variable number 0, even when the
input polynomial Q uses another variable:

  monomial(pp,p*i-1,0)

This agrees with the observation that x works and t fails. The same
expression is present in upstream master fetched on 2026-10-12, commit
d9f68890aee63df522bc0f69a913488e3fc3ffa7, at line 777.
